{"activity_text": "Antifungal, candidacidal, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (50%) to Pelophylaxin-4 G: 13%; L: 19%; K: 13%; R: 13%; Mol formula: C88H142N27O20; Mol Wt: 1897.252; Mol Ex Coeff: 5550; GRAVY: -0.34. Activity: active against C. albicans AY93025, C. albicans ATCC 10231, C. albicans CMCC 98001, C. albicans, 5 C. albicans clinical resistant strains (MIC 26.4-52.7 uM). It reduced biofilms as well. MOA:fungi: It increases ROS release in the yeast cell. It also disrupts mitochondrial membrane potential. Phibilin could induce C. albicans necrosis. Structure: helical in 25-75% TFE. DNA binding: It interacts with DNA based on gel retardation experiment. In vitro Toxicity: not hemo.lytic till 400 ug/ml. Not toxic to HEK293 or A549 cells till 200 ug/ml. Animal model:mouse: skin: fungus injected into the back skin and 1 h later injected with 50 ul (500 ug/ml) peptide at the infected site, once daily for 3 days. 2 logs CFU drop was observed.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "35633688", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2022 May 11;13:862834. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2022.862834. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03424", "source_id": "AP03424", "source_numeric_id": "03424", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03424", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In vitro and in vivo Activity of Phibilin Against Candida albicans", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
